<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ashanti Colony</h1><p class="st-meta">1902 CE – 1957 CE · capital Kumasi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British colony created from the conquered Ashanti Empire after the War of the Golden Stool, which joined independent Ghana in 1957.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>British forces occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a> in 1896 and exiled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asantehene">Asantehene</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prempeh-i">Prempeh I</a>, eventually to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-seychelles">Seychelles</a>. In 1900 the governor's demand for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-stool">Golden Stool</a>, the sacred symbol of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a> nation, provoked a rising led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaa-asantewaa">Yaa Asantewaa</a>, queen mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ejisu">Ejisu</a>. After its suppression <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> annexed Ashanti as a crown colony on 1 January 1902.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A chief commissioner at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a> governed through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a> chiefs. The colony became the heart of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gold-coast-colony">Gold Coast</a> cocoa production, and Kumasi grew into a major commercial centre linked by rail to the coast. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prempeh-i">Prempeh I</a> was allowed to return in 1924, and in 1935 the British restored the Asante <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederate-states-of-america">Confederacy</a> under his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prempeh-ii">Prempeh II</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 1950s the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-movement-ghana">National Liberation Movement</a>, based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a>, demanded a federal constitution, but on 6 March 1957 Ashanti became part of a unitary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asantehene">Asantehene</a> remains the most influential traditional ruler in the country.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1902 CE – 1957 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.55%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1902 CE – 1957 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kumasi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Prempeh I, Prempeh II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Akan traditional religion, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Asante Twi, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ghana">Ghana</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ashanti Crown Colony, Colony of Ashanti</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1930&amp;focus=ashanti-colony" aria-label="Ashanti Colony on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4635 1927 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ashanti Colony lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4955 2183L4973 2230M4955 2183L4997 651M4955 2183L4995 2226"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4973 2230h0M4997 651h0M4995 2226h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4955 2183h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4955 2183h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kumasi. <a href="/atlas?year=1930&amp;focus=ashanti-colony">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
